  "body": "﻿## What happens\n\nWhen a Rotary Flow (or the rotary twins) resolves its rotation axis, the resolved line has no readback: the machine editor shows the machine's stated rotary axis, the operation editor shows an operator-stated axis, but a fitted axis (the resolver's last step) is invisible in the UI. The fit's only traces are the band note's R figure and the heights' behaviour.\n\n## Why it matters\n\nA user who turns or moves a part cannot see where the fit landed, or whether it landed where they expect, until the cut is generated - and a wrong-axis surprise is a surprise at generation time, not at pick time.\n\n## Suggested behaviour\n\nShow the resolved axis in the operation editor for the rotary kinds: the source (machine / stated / fitted) and the line (a point and a direction, or \"through the work offset origin, direction X Y Z\"). Read-only is enough.\n\nSuggested labels: P7, area:ui, effort:low, source:agent.\r\n",
